# LucyK — Cursor Agent Rules

`AGENT.md` is the single source of truth for this repository. Read it in full, then read
`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/SYSCALL_ABI.md`, `docs/BSD_PERSONALITY.md`,
`docs/BSD_SYSCALLS.md`, and `CONTRIBUTING.md` before editing code under `src/` or `user/`.

## Non-negotiable rules

- Freestanding C11 only: `-std=c11 -ffreestanding -nostdlib -nostdinc -Wall -Wextra -Werror`
  plus `-mcmodel=kernel -mno-red-zone -mno-mmx -mno-sse -mno-sse2 -mno-80387`. Zero
  warnings; no libc.
- Zero POSIX/BSD identifiers in `src/mk/` or `src/arch/` — no `pid_t`, `fork`, `execve`,
  `vnode`, `inode`, `errno`, `bsd_*`, `BSD_*`, `sigaction`, `mprotect`, `pgid`.
- Zero `#include <bsd/...>` in `src/io/` (it is below `src/bsd/`).
- Zero Mach terminology — no `mach_*`, `kern_return_t`, `vm_map`, `pmap`, `task_self`,
  `bootstrap_port`.
- Zero stubs/TODOs — no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `HACK`, `XXX`, empty bodies, or fake returns.
- Strict `W^X`; route user memory through `copy_from_user`/`copy_to_user`; honor the lock
  hierarchy and `tlb_shootdown_mask()`.

## Before completing any task

Run the full gate and do not finish until it passes:

```bash
./scripts/verify.sh      # or: make verify
```

It covers: clean build (0 warnings), architectural boundary/hygiene scan, headless QEMU
boots on `-smp 1` and `-cpu max -smp 4` (Stage A–D self-tests, 0 leaked frames, `lucyk#`
prompt), and `e2fsck` filesystem integrity. Update the relevant `docs/` file whenever an
ABI or syscall changes.

## Git repository hygiene (mandatory)

Summary of `AGENT.md` §8 (Git Workflow & Branch Discipline) — `AGENT.md` remains the single
source of truth; this is not a replacement for the full spec. Every AI coding agent working
on `wylayss/lucyk` must:

- **never work on main — checkout feat/*, fix/*, audit/*, or docs/* first.** Run
  `git branch --show-current` before modifying any file; if it prints `main`, create and
  switch to a dedicated topic branch (`feat/<topic>`, `fix/<topic>`, `audit/<topic>`, or
  `docs/<topic>`).
- **Run `make verify` (`./scripts/verify.sh`) before committing.** Never create a commit
  until all four gates pass cleanly.
- **Use subsystem commit prefixes:** conventional commits scoped `mk:`, `arch:`, `io:`,
  `bsd:`, `user:`, `docs:`, or `chore:`. Syscall/ABI/locking-contract changes update
  `docs/*.md` in the same branch. Never stage build outputs (`build/`, `*.o`, `*.iso`,
  `*.img`).
- **Never auto-merge to `main`.** Merging into `main` and tagging releases are reserved for
  human maintainers after review. Never run `git push --force` or `git reset --hard` over
  unbacked local edits.
